<title>USA: Herman Miller Inc Q2 Nov 30 full results.</title>
<headline>Herman Miller Inc Q2 Nov 30 full results.</headline>
<dateline>ZEELAND, Mich. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Condensed Consolidated Statements</p>
<p>	   (Unaudited) (Dollars in 000s, except per share data)</p>
<p>						   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					     Nov. 30,	    Dec. 2,</p>
<p>						   1996		1995</p>
<p> Net Sales				 $377,137	   $328,393</p>
<p> Cost of Goods Sold		     242,837	    215,740</p>
<p> Gross Margin			     134,300	    112,653</p>
<p> Operating Expenses			97,430	     86,003</p>
<p> Patent Litigation Settlement/Other   5,500	     16,515</p>
<p> Operating Income			  31,370	     10,135</p>
<p> Other Expenses			     1,658		1,625</p>
<p> Income Before Taxes		     29,712		8,510</p>
<p> Taxes on Income			   11,860		3,555</p>
<p> Net Income			     17,852(a)	   4,955(b)</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share		    .74(a)	     .20(b)</p>
<p> Common Share Equivalents	  24,166,235	 25,188,041</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Includes $5.5 million write-off of $4.5 million, or $0.19/shr. (b) Includes $16.5 million pretax litigation settlements reducing net income $10.6 million, or $0.42/shr.</p>
<p>							 Six Months Ended</p>
<p>						Nov. 30,	    Dec. 2,</p>
<p>						    1996		1995</p>
<p> Net Sales				   $719,621	  $629,481</p>
<p> Cost of Goods Sold			 467,049	   413,949</p>
<p> Gross Margin				 252,572	   215,532</p>
<p> Operating Expenses			 188,612	   169,339</p>
<p> Patent Litigation Settlements/Other    5,500	    16,515</p>
<p> Operating Income			    58,460	    29,678</p>
<p> Other Expenses				 3,162	     2,254</p>
<p> Income Before Taxes			 55,298	    27,424</p>
<p> Taxes on Income			     21,860	    10,455</p>
<p> Net Income				 33,438(a)	 16,969(b)</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share		     1.38(a)	    .68(b)</p>
<p> Common Share Equivalents	    24,210,757	25,062,824</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Includes $5.5 million write-off that decreased net income by $4.5 million, or $0.19 per share. (b) Includes $16.5 million pretax litigation settlements which decreased net income by $10.6 million, or $0.42 per share.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
